NUMBERS: 
	each of these is a value type
----------------------------------------------
INTEGERS:
Types:
	sbyte: 
		signed 8-bit integer
		-128 to 127
	byte: 
		unsigned 8-bit integer
		0 to 255 
	short:
		signed 16-bit integer
		-32,768 to 32,767	
	ushort:
		unsigned 16-bit integer
		0 to 65,535	
	int:
		signed 32-bit integer
		-2,147,483,648 to 2,147,483,647	
	uint:
		unsigned 32-bit integer
		0 to 4,294,967,295	
	long:
		signed 64-bit integer
		-9,223,372,036,854,775,808 to 9,223,372,036,854,775,807	
	ulong:
		unsigned 64-bit integer
		0 to 18,446,744,073,709,551,615	
	nint:
		native signed integer (32 or 64 bit)
	nuint:
		native unsigned integer (32 or 64 bit)
			(to get min/max values at runtime use .MinValue/.MaxValue)
		
Integer Literals:
	decimal - default, no prefix (e.g. 42)
	hexadecimal - 0x or 0X prefix (e.g. 0x2A)
	binary - 0b or 0B prefix (e.g. 0b_0010_1010)
	
	they are always positive. can cast to other types to add signs
----------------------------------------------
FLOATING POINTS:
Types:
	float:
		4 bytes
		~6-9 digits
	double:
		8 bytes
		~15-17 digits
	decimal:
		16 bytes
		28-29 digits
		
Real Literals:
	double - d or D suffix (e.g. 3d)
	float - f or F suffix (e.g. 3.5F)
	decimal - m or M suffix (e.g. 400.75m)
	
	only float and double can be implicitly cast
----------------------------------------------
METHODS:
	Clamp(max value, min value) - clamps to the min/max inclusive
	CopySign(int A, int B) - copies sign from 'A' to 'B'
	Max(int A, int B) / Min(int A, int B) - returns the max/min value
	